Patch-Source: https://github.com/twisted/treq/pull/400
Upstream issues:
https://github.com/twisted/treq/issues/399
https://github.com/twisted/treq/issues/403
--
Alpine cannot depend on the `multipart` package (defnull/multipart): it
installs a top-level `multipart` module that collides with the one shipped
by py3-python-multipart (andrew-d/python-multipart), which is already in
community and provides a different API under the same import name.

Vendor the two helpers treq needs, as upstream PR #400 proposes.
Regenerated against 26.7.0; the previous version of this patch was written
against the setup.py-era tree and no longer applies.
--
